# Deny-by-default. This repo tracks ONLY the workspace definition and its
# own documentation. Everything else here — ten independent Meshtastic
# git repos, build caches, capture data — must never be committed.
#
# This is also what keeps Nix fast: for a flake in a git repo, Nix copies
# only TRACKED files into the store. Without the deny-all, evaluating the
# flake would copy the whole ~15 GB tree.
#
# NOTE: a new file is invisible to git until whitelisted below.
/*

# --- workspace definition -------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/.envrc
# CI. Both levels must be un-ignored: a negation cannot re-include a file if
# one of its parent directories is still excluded.
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
!/.github/workflows/*.yml
# Sourced from ~/.config/direnv/direnvrc. Tracked so a fresh machine inherits
# the `use nix` override that keeps firmware off upstream's broken platformio.
!/direnvrc
!/flake.nix
!/flake.lock
!/android-sdk-packages.txt
# The tool scripts the flake assembles into .#sync, .#worktree, .#brief,
# .#doctor and .#bootstrap-sdk. Real files so they are editable with shell
# tooling; must be tracked or pure eval cannot see them.
!/scripts/
!/scripts/*.sh
!/scripts/*.py
# Thin `just` aliases over the flake apps.
!/justfile
# The workspace plugin's hand-written source. sync renders it (plus generated
# forwarders) into .cache/agent-marketplace/, which stays ignored.
!/plugin/

# Paseo worktree config: setup command + on-demand scripts. Paseo reads this
# from the committed version of the base branch, so it must be tracked.
!/paseo.json

# --- documentation --------------------------------------------------------
# Policy, not a list: any markdown at the workspace root is workspace
# documentation and gets tracked. Covers README/AGENTS/CLAUDE plus the
# engineering notes (RCAs, bug handoffs) that would otherwise be lost.
# Notes belonging to a specific repo go in that repo instead.
!/*.md

# Workspace-local orientation notes for repos that publish no agent docs
# of their own (apple, protobufs, gradle-flatpak-sources, design,
# meshtastic-python), plus the material that belongs to no single repo
# (cross-repo-contracts.md, bench-fleet.md, node-inventory.md).
#
# Un-ignoring the DIRECTORY re-includes everything under it, not just the
# markdown: `/*` matches top-level entries only, so once `/notes` is back in,
# nothing below it is excluded again. The `*.md` line is therefore redundant
# — kept because it states the intent. Scratch tooling that lands here (soak
# scripts, capture json) is visible to git and must be deliberately committed
# or deliberately deleted; it will not be ignored for you.
!/notes/
!/notes/*.md

# --- explicitly excluded --------------------------------------------------
# Listed for the reader's benefit; /* already covers them.
#
#   .env          machine-local path exports, superseded by
#                 MESHTASTIC_WORKSPACE. No secrets, but not portable.
#   .cache/       workspace-local GRADLE_USER_HOME (multi-GB)
#   .direnv/      nix-direnv shell cache + GC roots
#   .ble-venv/    ad-hoc python venv
#   .remember/    agent scratch state
#   datasets/     packet captures
#   logs/         adb, build and replay logs
#   meshcon/      conference capture db + screenshots

# meshtastic-node-kmp is its own repo now (meshtastic/meshtastic-node-kmp),
# so it falls under the deny-all above like every other checkout here. It was
# tracked content until 2026-09-02; its history moved with it via subtree split.
__pycache__/
